CHECKER_PIN: the P3 message checker inside wasm-sol

Status: PIN SIGNED for the checker tree, with changes after the signature (listed below, not
signed). A P3 verifier signed the checker tree and its copy in this crate: p3delta-verdict.json
(verdict "pass-with-gaps"), the delta verifier of the P3 fix round. What it signed:
the verified-tree manifest 14b1ba4190989259e7d5ca49ba5250c7e10b6c9878c51892afda76ea61aaa5cc,
the pinned-tree manifest 59c3ac4af5e9c5f504f370e6f43eee087d398d61622871a9f659d07275a00fbf, the
seven files of the delta below, the copy of that tree in wasm-sol at the spike commit 18e7da7 with
the wasm df092b0eb130269db4c1e2c04c2e99093d3f456e0a97d93d566be7d87fe9b74d (982,473 bytes), and
the checker wasm of the P3 crate f7615f0fea44cff6000b1922eccfe196528b54540ff11c7368cd33dfb2225f61
(597,931 bytes). The verdict signs nothing else.

What this is. wasm-sol/src holds the source of the P3 checker crate (the scratch crate of step P3,
outside this repository). Every file is a byte for byte copy, except lib.rs and wasm.rs, which are
written new here (they add the modules and the entry points of wasm-sol), and the files that the
manifest marks `new`. The library keeps the name p3_check, so the tests are the P3 tests unchanged.

The verified tree. SHA-256 of the sorted manifest of the files that the verifier checked (src,
tests, tools, vectors and vendor of the P3 crate, with Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, clippy.toml and
rustfmt.toml): 14b1ba4190989259e7d5ca49ba5250c7e10b6c9878c51892afda76ea61aaa5cc
The verifier rebuilt the wasm of that tree: SHA-256 14f97e9b3f88c157199d7d6c61ca60e39dac23d6ab4e4a86353adea200743bef,
597,533 bytes, 267 tests, 83 rules.

