Changes of the move into the product repo (not signed; no file of src/ changed, so the rules and
the checker are those that the verdict signed):
- `zolana-hasher` is a copy of program-libs/hasher of the Zolana repo at commit 89640630, in
  vendor/zolana-hasher (Apache-2.0, see its LICENSE). Its src/ is byte for byte the source of the
  repo. Its Cargo.toml has the versions that the workspace of that repo sets, in place of
  `workspace = true`, and no dev-dependencies. Cargo.lock did not change.
- build.sh remaps the folder of the checkout to /zigs. The vendored crates sit inside the crate,
  so the wasm holds no path outside the repo, and the build gives the same bytes in any folder.
  The wasm differs from the one of the spike only in these path texts. The wasm hash above is
  of the new build.
- tests/repo_pins.rs: its tests are ignored. They read a checkout of the Zolana repo that the
  variable ZOLANA_REPO names. tests/common/mod.rs lost the two helpers that read that checkout
  (nothing used them).
- vectors: the funding address of the Devnet funder key is replaced by a test address in
  facts.json (`withdraw_recipient`) and in the messages that held it as an account key
  (p2/wire-*.msg, real/chain-withdraw.msg, real/work-report-fund.v.msg and
  real/work-withdraw-0.msg). The tests use that address only through facts.json and as an account
  of the message, so they hold as before. The wire files of landed transactions (*.wire, with
  signatures, used by no test) and account-sizes.json (used by no test) are dropped.
  vectors/roles.json holds four throwaway test seeds that tests/roles.rs compares with the
  values of the TS SDK. They belong to no Devnet account, and no spike key file holds them.

